title: Phantom53 ClickFix Delivery - MSI Installer Spawning PowerShell
id: 6406f2d4-c3e5-4410-b029-a438d379460f
status: experimental
description: Detects the execution pattern of the XaocMail ClickFix chain, where a Phantom53 MSI installer launched after a fake document-sharing lure spawns PowerShell to stage Havoc and communicate over DNS-over-HTTPS. Windows Installer spawning a PowerShell interpreter is rare enough for a high-signal hunt when paired with the campaign's installer lures.
references:
  - https://gbhackers.com/phantom53-malware-attack/
  - https://malware.news/t/xaocmail-clickfix-campaign-drops-phantom53-and-havox-across-latin-america-asia-and-europe/127279#post_1
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/11/17
tags:
  - attack.t1566
  - attack.t1204
  - attack.t1059
  - attack.t1071
logsource:
  category: process_creation
  product: windows
detection:
  selection_parent:
    ParentImage|endswith: '\msiexec.exe'
  selection_child:
    Image|endswith:
      - '\powershell.exe'
      - '\pwsh.exe'
  selection_flags:
    CommandLine|contains:
      - '-enc'
      - '-EncodedCommand'
      - '-nop'
      - '-w hidden'
      - '-WindowStyle Hidden'
  condition: selection_parent and selection_child and selection_flags
falsepositives:
  - Some legitimate enterprise MSI packages chain a PowerShell custom action; correlate with the installer path (user Downloads/Temp) and with subsequent outbound DoH or Tor traffic before escalating
level: medium
